This figure illustrates that Nano-11 enhances the expression of costimulatory molecules on dendritic cells (DCs). Flow cytometry analysis shows that bone marrow-derived DCs incubated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) for two days exhibit increased surface expression of CD40, and a marked increase in CD80 and CD86, compared to untreated control cells (gray line). This enhanced expression of costimulatory molecules indicates that Nano-11 activates DCs, a crucial step for initiating an effective immune response.